          },
          "text": "Vertically Merged Cells (Invisible Row Separators)"
        },
        {
          "attrs": {},
          "bbox": {
            "page": 0,
            "x0": 78,
            "x1": 508,
            "y0": 127,
            "y1": 136
          },
          "children": [],
          "id": "ad92710106f2",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "provenance": {
            "extractor": "segment",
            "stage": "build_tree"
          },
          "text": "The first column visually merges three rows because the inner row dividers are drawn in the page"
        },
        {
          "attrs": {},
          "bbox": {
            "page": 0,
            "x0": 79,
            "x1": 496,
            "y0": 139,
            "y1": 148
          },
          "children": [],
          "id": "36e8fe608b08",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "provenance": {
            "extractor": "segment",
            "stage": "build_tree"
          },
          "text": "background colour. A reader sees one merged cell containing three lines of text; the PDF data,"
        },
        {
          "attrs": {},
          "bbox": {
            "page": 0,
            "x0": 79,
            "x1": 520,
            "y0": 151,
            "y1": 160
          },
          "children": [],
          "id": "da52804ea6cc",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "provenance": {
            "extractor": "segment",
            "stage": "build_tree"
          },
          "text": "however, still encodes three separate rows split by white-on-white lines. A colour-aware parser must"
        },
        {
          "attrs": {},
          "bbox": {
            "page": 0,
            "x0": 79,
            "x1": 192,
            "y0": 163,
            "y1": 172
          },
          "children": [],
          "id": "7d7a24447fb0",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "provenance": {
            "extractor": "segment",
            "stage": "build_tree"
          },
          "text": "honour the visual reading."
        },
